From b97ad18b0aae444261c08e535403237413081a75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TrustMate Driver App <noreply@trustmate.app>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:53:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix inspection capture-loss bug, redesign shot list, and
 pending fixes

- Photos are now uploaded immediately as each is captured (draft path) and
  persisted to AsyncStorage, so the native camera killing the app mid
  walkaround no longer loses already-taken shots and dumps the driver back
  at Home.
- Inspection shot list restructured into a full directional walkaround:
  Front, Front Driver Side, Driver Side, Back Driver Side, Back, Back
  Passenger Side, Passenger Side, Front Passenger Side (exterior) plus
  Dashboard, Front Seats, Back Seats, Boot/Trunk (interior). Every shot has
  its own illustrated diagram so drivers who can't read the labels can
  still recognize the angle.
- check-inspection-photo and analyze-inspection edge functions updated to
  match the new 12-shot key list (server-side, already deployed).
- Also includes previously-delivered but not-yet-applied fixes: real-time
  per-photo quality/match gate during capture, reference-photo cache
  staleness fix, trip-tracking permission-denial banner, missing expo-font
  peer dependency.
